<title>UK: European cotton markets very quiet due to holiday.</title>
<headline>European cotton markets very quiet due to holiday.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in the European raw cotton markets was subdued due to the celebration of All Saint day, sources said.</p>
<p>With harvests underway at several major production centres and uncertainty over the quality of the new cotton, spinners are proving reluctant to buy forward beyond the winter shipment period, they said.</p>
<p>The volume of new business reported was minimal, they added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
